cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Nabla in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "Nabla: A Chess Engine That Chooses Moves by Energy Descent on Ray-Transport Fields"
abstract: >-
  Nabla is a chess engine that chooses moves by energy descent on
  ray-transport fields. Each piece emits
  influence along its exact attack rays, attenuated by blocking pieces so that
  direct control is separated from X-ray pressure. Every evaluation decomposes
  exactly into named terms. Moves are chosen by steepest ascent of the energy on
  the game graph, with optional capture-only or one-reply lookahead, and playing
  strength is controlled by a Boltzmann temperature calibrated to Elo.
authors:
  - given-names: Sreecharan
    family-names: S.
    alias: sr2echa
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - chess engine
  - ray transport
  - low-search chess
  - Rust
  - WebAssembly
